<%- include("_head", { title: "JSL-online (SP)" }) %>

<h1>JSL-online (SP)</h1>

<p id="status">Not signed in.</p>

<p><a href="/login">Sign in through Demo OpenAM</a></p>

<h2>SAML endpoints this SP exposes</h2>
<ul>
    <li><code>GET /api/saml/metadata</code> — SP metadata, to be registered with the IdP</li>
    <li><code>POST /api/saml/acs</code> — receives the SAMLResponse delivered by the IdP</li>
</ul>

<h2>Its own API</h2>
<ul>
    <li><code>GET /api/me</code> — requires <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;jwt&gt;</code></li>
</ul>

<script>
    // Whether a token is present says nothing about whether it is still valid; only
    // /api/me can answer that. This is just a hint on the landing page.
    if (localStorage.getItem("sp_access_token")) {
        document.getElementById("status").textContent =
            "An access token is present — open /profile to have it verified.";
    }
</script>

